Z||000006||william_thorniii||12-22-1999||06:01 PM||||56... <P>Head gasket failure is quite common on the Iron Duke.  It is fairly accessable, but most people don't like the thought of tearing down most of their engine to do it... even though it only costs them $30 (for the high performance) replacement part.  Quite often you will see people selling cars with bad head gaskets for darn near nothing.  <P>Dogtired.... <P>I usually have a habit of offering to buy just parts off of cars in this shape, or buy the whole thing for just parts... Sometimes you can buy a car for $100 remove $500 of parts that you would have to otherwise buy and sell the remainder to the bone-yard (which they usually come and pick up.. even if you keep the wheels) for another $50.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||12-22-1999||06:03 PM||||OOOOOOPS! I forgot to mention that many aftermarket wings were/are one piece. Chris Cook out of Indy used to sell wings for $150 and they were one piece including the stantions.  Yes that is right... they were $150 new ready to paint, but he DOES NOT make them any longer.... bummer huh?<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
